course: dictionary
lesson: 12314
title: Correspondence: letters and matches
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Correspondence is a word for letters, emails and messages that people send to each other. «Mum reads her correspondence every morning» means she reads the letters and emails that have arrived for her.
explain: Correspondence can also mean writing to each other over a long time. «Ella and her pen-friend kept up a correspondence for years» means they wrote letters to each other for many years.
explain: Correspondence can also mean a close match between two things. «There is a one-to-one correspondence between the chairs and the children» means every chair has exactly one child sitting on it, and every child has exactly one chair.
fact: Correspondence means letters, emails or messages sent between people.
fact: «Correspondence» can mean writing to each other over time, like a long letter friendship.
fact: In business and formal writing, correspondence often means mail.
fact: In maths, a one-to-one correspondence pairs each item in one set with exactly one item in another set.
fact: Letters between famous people are called their correspondence, and historians like to read them.
exercise: «She reads her correspondence every morning.» What is her correspondence? | Her favourite songs | Her pets and their food | *Her letters and emails | Her school bags
exercise: «We kept up a correspondence for years.» What does this mean? | We ran a race together | We shared one bedroom | *We wrote letters to each other for a long time | We stopped talking straight away
exercise: «Each child has one cup, so there is a one-to-one correspondence between the children and the cups.» What does one-to-one correspondence mean? | There are more cups than children | The cups are all the same colour | Each child has three cups | *Each item is paired with exactly one item in the other set
test: «The office keeps all its correspondence in a grey filing cabinet.» What does correspondence mean here? | Food for lunch | *Letters and business mail | Maps of the moon | Pencils and rubbers
test: «Sam's list of names has a close correspondence with the list of numbers.» What does correspondence mean here? | A loud noise in the hall | *A close match or link between the two lists | A fight between two friends | A long walk to school
exam: «Their correspondence filled a whole shoebox.» What does correspondence mean in this sentence? | *Letters and messages sent between them | Lunch packed in a bag | Boxes of old toys | Shoes for school
